<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coup of Rucunshu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rucunshu coup</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Coup of Rucunshu was a succession struggle at the Rwandan court in late 1896. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kigeli-iv-rwabugiri">Kigeli IV Rwabugiri</a>, his chosen heir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mibambwe-iv-rutarindwa">Mibambwe IV Rutarindwa</a> was attacked at Rucunshu by the faction of the queen mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanjogera">Kanjogera</a> and her brothers, and died with many of his supporters. Kanjogera's young son was installed as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuhi-v-musinga">Yuhi V Musinga</a>, leaving power with her Bega clan.</p></div>
